description:
LIFECYCLE EVENT BUS (P2): Current events.rs has EventType enum with 13 variants (AgentRegistered/Started/Progress/Blocked/Completed/Failed/Crashed/Stopped/Replaced/HandoffCreated/PromptStalled/Rejected + WorkSubmitted/Verified/Accepted/Rejected/ReviewEscalated). Need comprehensive lifecycle events.

NEW EVENT TYPES:
- PeerSpawned { peer_id, pid, workspace, disposition }
- PeerReady { peer_id }
- PeerCrashed { peer_id, exit_code, signal, workspace_lease_id }
- PeerStopped { peer_id, reason }
- TaskReceived { task_id, assigned_to }
- TaskExecuting { task_id, peer_id }
- TaskCompleted { task_id, peer_id }
- TaskFailed { task_id, peer_id, error }
- VerificationStarted { task_id, profile }
- VerificationPassed { task_id, evidence_id }
- VerificationFailed { task_id, findings }
- WorkspaceAcquired { lease_id, path, holder }
- WorkspaceReleased { lease_id }
- WorkspaceCleaned { lease_id }
- LeadHandoff { from_lead, to_lead, reason }

EVENT BUS ARCHITECTURE:
- EventBus struct with handlers: HashMap<EventType, Vec<Box<dyn Handler>>>
- emit(event) → dispatch to all registered handlers
- Handler trait: fn handle(&self, event: &Event) -> Result<()>
- RecoveryHandler: on PeerCrashed → cleanup workspace
- EvidenceHandler: on VerificationPassed → persist EvidenceRecord
- NotificationHandler: on events → log to SQLite + optional webhook

FILES:
- crates/anti-core/src/events.rs — expand EventType enum
- crates/anti-daemon/src/bus.rs (NEW) — EventBus, Handler trait, built-in handlers

INTEGRATION:
- Replace direct emit_event() calls with EventBus.emit()
- Register handlers at daemon startup
- Recovery handler wired to TreehouseAdapter

Tests:
- emit PeerCrashed → RecoveryHandler called
- emit VerificationPassed → EvidenceHandler called
- emit without handler → no panic (log warning)
